I would reject the "computer storage" part, because 
bits are also spoken of, and retain their meaning, in 
theoretical discussions.  Even tho in these theoretical 
discussions it is understood that there is (typically) 
a physical realization of the theory being discussed.

And besides, a "computer", in everyday non-Lojban
usage at least, is quite a bit more complicated than 
the minimum-size device that can and does use "bits".

Again, I would not tie the lujvo for "bit" to any sort 
of technology at all; it would be both necessary and 
sufficient merely to *imply* a physical realization.

Hope this doesn't muddy the waters ?? ..

